  "notes": [
    "[GENERAL] Culinary grade matcha is made from tea leaves harvested later than ceremonial grade leaves, producing a bolder, more robust flavor profile that holds up well against milk, sweeteners, and baking ingredients.",
    "[GENERAL] When preparing matcha drinks, use hot water heated to around 160°F to 175°F (70°C to 80°C), as boiling water can scorch the delicate tea leaves and intensify bitterness.",
    "[GENERAL] For a smooth, clump-free texture in lattes and beverages, sift 1/2 to 1 teaspoon of powder into a bowl or mug, add 2 ounces of warm water, and whisk rapidly in a zig-zag \"W\" or \"M\" motion before stirring in milk or other liquids.",
    "[GENERAL] Flavored culinary matcha powders are versatile additions to hot or iced lattes, smoothies, protein shakes, and baked goods like cookies, frostings, and cakes.",
    "[GENERAL] Finely ground green tea powder degrades quickly when exposed to heat, air, and light; store it tightly sealed in a cool, dark place or in the refrigerator to keep the flavor and aroma fresh."
